-### NV Rendering Formula (Trilerp)
-Implements an 'NV' rendering formula using trilinear interpolation (trilerp) [S2, unofficial]. Includes forward, backward, and fused variants [S2, unofficial]. The forward variant computes the output tensor directly [S2, unofficial]. The backward variant computes gradients for the grid output [S2, unofficial]. The fused variant combines the forward pass with additional parameters and computes gradients [S2, unofficial].
-
-## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** Improved over standard trilinear interpolation due to SIMD parallelism [S1].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** Reduced cache misses due to bit-interleaved block decomposition ($32^3$ samples) [S1].
-*   **Strengths:** Faster interpolation and memory copying on supported hardware [S1].
-*   **Limitations:** Artifacts on MMX-only processors [S1].
-*   **When to use:** When rendering performance is critical and the target hardware supports MMX, SSE, or 3DNow! [S1].
-*   **When not to use:** On MMX-only processors if artifacts are unacceptable [S1].
+**When to Use:**
+- Use when hardware supports MMX, SSE, or 3DNow! SIMD extensions and performance optimization is critical [S1].
+- Avoid on MMX-only processors if artifact-free rendering is required [S1].
 
 ## Background
-The method was introduced in "A new object-order ray-casting algorithm" [S1]. It leverages existing SIMD processor extensions to optimize volume rendering performance [S1]. The bit-interleaved addressing scheme is also described in this work [S1].
-
+Optimized Trilinear Reconstruction was introduced in the paper "A new object-order ray-casting algorithm" [S1]. It builds on the principles of trilinear interpolation and applies SIMD optimizations to enhance performance in direct volume ray casting.
